# Troop <NUMBER>

Troop <NUMBER> is a Scouting America troop in <CITY>, <STATE>.

## Calendar feed (`TROOP_CALENDAR_URL`)

    <https://calendar.google.com/calendar/ical/... or other published iCal feed URL>

## Badge inventory sheet (`BADGE_INVENTORY_URL`)

    <https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/<SHEET_ID>/edit>

The Google Sheet tracking how many rank patches, pins, position patches, awards,
and merit badge patches the troop has on hand.  It must be shared as "anyone
with the link can view" — the `badge-inventory` skill reads it over plain HTTP
with no Google credentials.  Each tab needs the columns `Count`, `Last Checked`,
`Checked by`, and `Notes` after its own label column.

## Current Patrols (as of <YYYY-MM-DD>)

| Patrol | Nickname | Notes |
| :----- | :------- | :---- |
| <Patrol Name> | <Nickname> | <e.g. age range or other notes> |
| <Patrol Name> | <Nickname> | <e.g. age range or other notes> |

## Previous Patrols (include but not limited to)

| Patrol | Retired | Notes |
| :----- | :------ | :---- |
| <Patrol Name> | <e.g. Summer 2026> | <what happened to its members> |

Additionally, the "<Adult Patrol Name>" is the adult scoutmaster patrol.  Note
any naming quirks that could be confused with a youth patrol.

## How the troop runs advancement

These apply to any advancement planning — rank or merit badge, Target First
Class or Target Eagle:

- **Abbreviations** — note any troop-specific shorthand (e.g. "SMC" for
  Scoutmaster Conference and "BoR" for Board of Review).
- **Scoutmaster conferences and boards of review** — describe whether/how they
  appear on the calendar (e.g. inside regular meetings vs. scheduled
  separately).
- **Per-meeting capacity** — describe the real constraint on how many
  conferences or boards can be scheduled per meeting, and whether they can run
  concurrently.
- **Who can sign off what** — describe which adult roles can sign off merit
  badge requirements, run boards of review, and run Scoutmaster conferences.
- **Any standard shorthand for the closing rank requirements** (Scout Spirit,
  Scoutmaster conference, board of review).
- **Any recurring troop-specific events** relevant to advancement planning
  (e.g. an intensive sign-off day) — describe format, duration, adult
  leader turnout, and how much of the conference/board load it typically
  absorbs.
